### Cross-Boundary State Synchronization

When micro-frontends share a page, coordinating authentication tokens, tenant contexts, and user profiles without tight coupling requires event-driven communication patterns.

#### Communication Topologies
1. **Custom Event Bus**: Leverages the native browser `CustomEvent` API with strongly typed payloads.
2. **BroadcastChannel API**: Facilitates cross-tab or cross-frame messaging across isolated contexts.
3. **Decoupled State Broker**: A pub/sub broker instantiated at the shell level that exposes scoped subscriptions.

```javascript
// Enterprise Event Broker for Micro-Frontends
class CrossAppMessageBroker {
  constructor() {
    this.handlers = new Map();
  }

  subscribe(topic, callback) {
    if (!this.handlers.has(topic)) {
      this.handlers.set(topic, new Set());
    }
    this.handlers.get(topic).add(callback);
    return () => this.handlers.get(topic).delete(callback);
  }

  publish(topic, payload) {
    if (this.handlers.has(topic)) {
      const immutablePayload = Object.freeze({ ...payload, timestamp: Date.now() });
      this.handlers.get(topic).forEach(handler => {
        try {
          handler(immutablePayload);
        } catch (err) {
          console.error(`Broker error on topic [${topic}]:`, err);
        }
      });
    }
  }
}
```

#### Security Considerations
Never expose raw write handles to administrative state across third-party remote components. Validate schemas at every subscriber boundary.

