### Transport Selection: WebSockets vs SSE vs HTTP/3 WebTransport

Choosing the correct protocol for live data updates directly impacts memory utilization, battery consumption, and proxy pass-through rates.

| Feature | WebSockets | Server-Sent Events (SSE) | WebTransport |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Directionality** | Full-Duplex (Bidirectional) | Simplex (Server-to-Client) | Full-Duplex Multiplexed |
| **Transport** | TCP (Upgrade handshake) | HTTP/1.1 or HTTP/2 | UDP (QUIC) |
| **Auto Reconnect** | Manual implementation | Native browser handling | Protocol-level recovery |
| **Firewall Traversal** | Blocked by some enterprise proxies | Standard HTTP streaming | Native QUIC handling |

#### Production Resilient SSE Client

```javascript
function connectEventStream(endpoint, onMessage, onError) {
  const eventSource = new EventSource(endpoint, { withCredentials: true });

  eventSource.onmessage = (event) => {
    try {
      const payload = JSON.parse(event.data);
      onMessage(payload);
    } catch (parseError) {
      console.error('Invalid SSE frame JSON:', parseError);
    }
  };

  eventSource.onerror = (err) => {
    if (eventSource.readyState === EventSource.CLOSED) {
      console.warn('Stream closed by server.');
    }
    onError(err);
  };

  return () => eventSource.close();
}
```

