### Ignition, TurboFan, and Inline Caches (IC)

The V8 JavaScript engine utilizes a multi-tier compilation pipeline to balance fast startup latency with peak execution speed.

#### Engine Pipeline Phases
1. **Parser**: Converts source code into an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST).
2. **Ignition Interpreter**: Generates memory-efficient bytecode from the AST for immediate execution.
3. **Profiler**: Identifies hot functions and collects type feedback vectors.
4. **TurboFan Optimizing Compiler**: Compiles hot bytecode into highly optimized machine code based on recorded type assumptions.

#### Hidden Classes & Object Shapes
JavaScript objects are dynamically typed, but V8 internally models them with rigid transition graphs termed **Hidden Classes** (or Shapes).

```javascript
// Monomorphic property initialization (Optimal Shape consistency)
function createPoint(x, y) {
  this.x = x;
  this.y = y;
}

const p1 = new createPoint(10, 20); // Shape A -> Shape B
const p2 = new createPoint(30, 40); // Shape A -> Shape B (Reuses same shape)

// Polymorphic deoptimization anti-pattern:
const p3 = {};
p3.y = 20; // Starts with property y
p3.x = 10; // Shape differs from p1/p2, causing inline cache miss
```

