### Three-Tier Token Architecture for Enterprise Design Systems

Scalable CSS architecture decouples raw values from component consumption using a three-tier token hierarchy:

1. **Global (Primitive) Tokens**: Raw palette and scale values (`--color-blue-600: #2563eb;`, `--space-4: 1rem;`).
2. **Semantic (Alias) Tokens**: Contextual roles (`--color-surface-primary`, `--color-border-focus`, `--color-text-brand`).
3. **Component Tokens**: Scoped to specific elements (`--btn-padding-x`, `--card-elevation-shadow`).

```css
:root {
  /* 1. Primitive */
  --blue-500: #3b82f6;
  --slate-900: #0f172a;
  --slate-100: #f1f5f9;

  /* 2. Semantic Default (Light) */
  --bg-canvas: #ffffff;
  --text-primary: var(--slate-900);
  --border-subtle: #e2e8f0;
}

[data-theme="dark"] {
  /* Semantic Dark Overrides */
  --bg-canvas: var(--slate-900);
  --text-primary: var(--slate-100);
  --border-subtle: #334155;
}

/* 3. Component Token Scoping */
.ui-button {
  --btn-bg: var(--blue-500);
  background-color: var(--btn-bg);
  color: #ffffff;
  padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem;
  border-radius: 6px;
}
```

