### Container Queries: Beyond Global Viewports

Traditional `@media` queries bind element styling to the total viewport width, which breaks modularity when components are placed in narrow sidebars or flexible dashboard grids.

Container queries allow components to inspect and react to the dimensions of their immediate parent container.

```css
.dashboard-widget {
  container-type: inline-size;
  container-name: widget-card;
}

@container widget-card (min-width: 480px) {
  .widget-content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
}

@container widget-card (max-width: 479px) {
  .widget-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
}
```

